### Verification trail (seven independent checks, all run 2026-10-24)

1. **Artificial Analysis:** `https://artificialanalysis.ai/models/neomorph` returns **404** — no model page.
2. **Hugging Face model search** (`https://huggingface.co/models?search=neomorph`): returns literally **"No results found"** — zero models, zero orgs. This is the decisive negative: HF hosts essentially every open-weights model, so a zero-result search rules out any public checkpoint.
3. **OpenRouter** (`https://openrouter.ai/models?q=neomorph`): the page rendered its default recent-models list (Kimi K3.1 Pro, Flint, Mammoth 1, Nemotron, MiniMax M3.1 Flash, DeepSeek V4.1 Flash…) with **no `neomorph` route or model anywhere** in the rendered set.
4. **models.dev canonical table:** browsed the full ~14,000-line canonical-model table (covering Meta, Nvidia, Google, OpenAI, Anthropic, DeepSeek, MiniMax, Xiaomi, Upstage, InclusionAI, StepFun, mistralai, alibaba, quiverai, sakana, vivgrid, unbiased, typesafe, aleph-alpha, phocinae, meituan, lightonai and the rest of the tracked labs). A string search for "neomorph" returned **no match** — not as a model, not as a lab name, not as a slug.
5. **Bing** for `"Neomorph" AI model LLM benchmarks`: 57 results, but every visible hit is `mybroadband.co.za` — a South African internet-speed-test site (speedtest pages, 5G articles, Telkom/Rain forum threads). Zero AI-model pages, zero benchmark-tracker entries.
6. **Bing** for `"Neomorph" LLM open weights OR checkpoint OR "model card"`: claims 14,700 results, but every visible hit is a generic LLM directory that never mentions a model called Neomorph (`opensourcesai.com/models`, `computingforgeeks.com`, an HF blog post, `theopenweights.com`, `benchlm.ai`, `morphllm.com/models`, `opensourceaimodels.net`, `llm-releases.com`). Bing silently dropped the quoted keyword, so the result set is not evidence either way — noted as a low-quality check. (Note `morphllm.com` is a *different* product, Morph LLM, and was not confused with this slug.)
7. **Google** for `"Neomorph" LLM model`: blocked — returned Google's JS-retry error page with no result content. Recorded as an inconclusive check and not used as evidence.

### Conflict / resolution notes

- No conflicting sources were found. The four neutral sources — Artificial Analysis (404), Hugging Face (0 results), OpenRouter (absent) and models.dev (no match) — all agree independently that nothing exists under this name. The three noisy checks (two Bing searches and a blocked Google) are individually disclosed above and are not counted as evidence.
- **Strictness note:** "Neomorph" is a common word outside AI, so a much higher evidentiary bar was applied than for the other phantom slugs in this queue. Nothing that qualifies was found — no model card, no weights repo, no API route, no gateway listing, no benchmark-tracker entry, and not even a passing mention in a genuine model listing.
- **Surfaced for the orchestrator, not acted on:** this slug appears in `model-queue.md` with a computed Overall of 52, so other raters evidently produced reports for it. Under `RULES.md` a folder is permanent and only a *user* may park a slug (it must be removed from both `RETIRED_SLUGS` lists, `src/data/models.ts` + `scripts/lib/average.mjs`, to be rendered in `model-aliases.generated.md`). This file therefore makes no parking recommendation and no deletion — it records the negative finding and stops.
- **Batch note:** this is the seventh phantom slug found in this queue and the second (`owo-2.5` being the other) where the *word itself* is common outside AI. Both are the weakest-evidence phantoms in the set, because a common word guarantees SEO noise; the Hugging Face zero-result search and the models.dev no-match are what make the negative conclusion solid for both.

